# Faviax Universe Website

## Business Requirements

* An immersive single-page web application (Landing Page) for the Faviax sci-fi universe.
* The web app should showcase the lore, history, and link to all digital music platforms.
* The design must feel like accessing a classified archive from the future or a cyberpunk terminal.
* The priority is a slick, professional, dark-mode UI/UX with an engaging "Glassmorphism" style.
* Must include clear spaces for future custom images and artwork.

## Technical Details

* Implemented as a modern single-page dark mode experience.
* Typography: Futuristic geometric fonts for headings (e.g., Orbitron, Syncopate) and monospaced fonts for subtitles/metadata (e.g., Roboto Mono).
* The layout must be divided into 5 distinct sections: Hero (Start), Archive Access (Lore grid), Transmissions (Music layout), Chronicles (Timeline), and Connect (Network links).
* Cards and containers should feature subtle borders that glow on hover.
* Section dividers should use thin dotted or solid lines.

## Color Scheme

* Main Background: Very dark space purple/blue (`#0B0710` to `#120A1A`).
* Cyan/Neon Primary: `#00F3FF` - primary buttons, music links, glows.
* Purple/Magenta Secondary: `#B026FF` or `#8A2BE2` - subtitles, card borders, decorative elements.
* White Main Text: `#FFFFFF` - for high legibility.
* Gray/Blue Secondary Text: `#A0A5B5` - supporting text.

## Strategy

1. Build the Hero Section with a full-screen cyberpunk background placeholder, centered massive title, and two neon Call to Action buttons.
2. Develop "The Signal" section using a 3-column grid for lore cards (image on top, neon title, short paragraph).
3. Create the "Transmissions" section with a 2-column layout (featured album art on the left, tracklist and minimalist streaming platform icons on the right).
4. Implement the "Neo-Astra Chronicles" as a vertical timeline or zigzag layout highlighting key dates in cyan next to historical text and panorama image placeholders.
5. Finish with the "Connect" section using a 4-column grid for social/community buttons with hover glow effects, ending with a minimal footer.

## Coding Standards

1. Image Formats: Use WebP or high-quality compressed JPGs to ensure deep blacks without pixelation.
2. Transparency: Use PNG with transparent backgrounds for isolated elements (characters, ships) in the timeline and music sections.
3. Consistency: Ensure all image placeholders and color filters strictly respect the purple and cyan core palette.